    "updated_at": "2018-02-25T13:37:26Z",
    "body": "Note to whoever reviews \"Participation\" - I have signed up as an individual; in so doing, I have chosen not to read \"work in the field of web technologies\" too broadly; but a broader reading might require me to get my employer to sign up.  I work for The Qt Company on the Qt framework, which does include some implementations of web technologies (classes to make REST and http(2|s|) requests and for use in implementing servers), which I do work on; however, these are just standard parts of most modern software and Qt is not specifically a web technology, as such.  If you disagree with that reading, I'll need to talk to my bosses about whether TQtC is willing to sign up, which may run into management not thinking we're a web technology company ...\r\n\r\nIn any case, I make this contribution as a private individual, outside the scope of my work and reasonably believe my employer has neither any basis in law for objecting to my doing so nor any inclination to so object.",
